From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:09:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sf_smac: let a failed probe fail

When the LMAC did not come up at probe, the driver scheduled a reprobe
of itself, and so did every reprobe after it. Each round loads the
firmware, allocates the IPC rings and runs the user-mode helper, so a
board whose firmware does not start (a mismatched LMAC image, say) runs
out of memory within seconds instead of reporting the error.

Return the error from probe. Keep the reprobe that recovers a radio
which failed at run time, but give up after three per module load.

Found on the Banana Pi BPI-WiFi5 by the napoluluna/bpi-wifi5-openwrt
port.

Signed-off-by: Joseph Telaak <joseph@telaak.dev>
---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_main.c | 4 +---
 sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mpw0.c         | 8 ++++++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_main.c b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_main.c
index e9ec102..44a35ef 100644
--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_main.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/fullmac/siwifi_main.c
@@ -4081,10 +4081,8 @@ int siwifi_cfg80211_init(struct siwifi_plat *siwifi_plat, void **platform_data)
   siwifi_hw->skb_pool_dev_param->use_skb_pool = 1;
  }
 #endif
-    if ((ret = siwifi_platform_on(siwifi_hw))) {
-        siwifi_reprobe_driver(siwifi_hw);
+    if ((ret = siwifi_platform_on(siwifi_hw)))
         goto err_platon;
-    }
     if (siwifi_ipc_elem_var_allocs(siwifi_hw, &siwifi_hw->dying_gasp_info_elem,
                 sizeof(struct mm_dying_gasp), DMA_FROM_DEVICE,
                 NULL, NULL, ipc_host_dying_gasp_addr_push, NULL))
diff --git a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mpw0.c b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mpw0.c
index 61a2fd8..8b56127 100644
--- a/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mpw0.c
+++ b/sf_smac/src/bb_src/umac/siwifi_mpw0.c
@@ -81,11 +81,19 @@ void siwifi_reprobe_work(struct work_struct *wk)
 #endif
     SIWIFI_DBG(SIWIFI_FN_EXIT_STR);
 }
+/* Recovery reprobes per module load before the radio is left dead. */
+#define SIWIFI_REPROBE_MAX 3
+static atomic_t siwifi_reprobe_count = ATOMIC_INIT(0);
 void siwifi_reprobe_driver(struct siwifi_hw *siwifi_hw)
 {
     struct siwifi_reprobe *reprobe;
     printk("siwifi_reprobe_driver\n");
     set_bit(SIWIFI_DEV_HW_DEAD, &siwifi_hw->drv_flags);
+    if (atomic_inc_return(&siwifi_reprobe_count) > SIWIFI_REPROBE_MAX) {
+        printk(KERN_CRIT "%s: gave up after %d reprobes\n", __func__,
+               SIWIFI_REPROBE_MAX);
+        return;
+    }
     if (!try_module_get(THIS_MODULE)) {
         printk(KERN_CRIT "%s: Module is being unloaded - abort\n", __func__);
         return;
